LearnLoop: third-party notices
==============================

The app itself is licensed AGPL-3.0-or-later (see LICENSE, in this same folder).

The LearnLoop mobile app bundles the third-party libraries listed below into its builds, and this
file reproduces their notices: for each library, its name, its version, its licence as its
package.json states it, and the copyright lines of its LICENSE file where the package ships one.
The full licence text of each library is in the LICENSE file of its package as published on npm.

How this list was made (2026-10-01): the app's JavaScript bundle was built for iOS and for
Android with `expo export --source-maps`, and every package with a file in either source map
is listed under "App bundle". The Strudel player's page is built by
scripts/build-strudel.mjs from @strudel/web, whose published file dist/index.mjs
already contains its dependencies; the packages under "Strudel player page" are @strudel/web's
dependency tree as installed from pnpm-lock.yaml, without the type-only @types packages.
Native libraries that React Native and Expo compile into the app from CocoaPods and Gradle,
outside the JavaScript bundle, are not listed here.


Strudel
-------

Strudel (@strudel/web 1.3.0, the other @strudel packages, superdough and supradough, listed
under "Strudel player page") is licensed AGPL-3.0-or-later. Source:
https://codeberg.org/uzu/strudel. The @kabelsalat packages there are AGPL-3.0-or-later too. The
app bundles Strudel into the Strudel player's page (src/strudel/generated/strudelHtml.ts, written
at build time), whose script starts with the comment
"@strudel/web 1.3.0 | AGPL-3.0-or-later | https://codeberg.org/uzu/strudel".

Rule REPO-7 (AGENTS.md, docs/standards.md): a distribution build (preview, TestFlight or App
Store) is made only once the exact source it was built from is published under its tag
(docs/publishing.md).


